%N A402467 Number of essential acyclic digraphs (or DAGs) on n labeled nodes in which every node has in-degree at most 3.
%C A402467 An acyclic digraph is essential if it is the only member of its Markov equivalence class, that is, if no other acyclic digraph has the same skeleton and the same v-structures (a -> c <- b with a and b not adjacent); see Andersson, Madigan and Perlman.
%C A402467 Equivalently, by a theorem of Chickering, it has no covered arc: an arc u -> v is covered if the parents of v are u together with the parents of u.
%C A402467 Equivalently, a(n) is the number of Bayesian network structures on n variables, each variable with at most 3 parents, that are the only acyclic digraph on these variables with their conditional independence relations.
%C A402467 Without the bound on the in-degree the count is A026586. With in-degree at most 1 it is 1 for every n, since an arc out of a root of a rooted forest is covered.
%C A402467 a(n) = A026586(n) for n <= 4; a(5) = 2341 against A026586(5) = 2616.
%D A402467 R. W. Robinson, Counting labeled acyclic digraphs, in F. Harary, ed., New Directions in the Theory of Graphs, Academic Press, NY, 1973, pp. 239-273.
%H A402467 Tyler Satchel Orden, <a href="/A402467/b402467.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..30</a>
%H A402467 Steen A. Andersson, David Madigan and Michael D. Perlman, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1214/aos/1031833662">A characterization of Markov equivalence classes for acyclic digraphs</a>, Ann. Statist., 25 (1997), 505-541.
%H A402467 Davide Bizzaro, Luciano Serafini and Sagar Malhotra, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.13736">Towards Counting Markov Equivalence Classes with Logical Constraints</a>, arXiv:2405.13736 [cs.LO], 2024. See Table 1.
%H A402467 David Maxwell Chickering, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1302.4938">A Transformational Characterization of Equivalent Bayesian Network Structures</a>, arXiv:1302.4938 [cs.AI], 2013; Proc. 11th Conf. on Uncertainty in Artificial Intelligence (UAI 1995), 87-98.
%H A402467 Bertran Steinsky, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/S0012-365X(02)00838-5">Enumeration of labelled chain graphs and labelled essential directed acyclic graphs</a>, Discrete Math., 270 (2003), 267-278.
%F A402467 Let E(n,i,j,l) be the number of these digraphs with exactly i, j and l nodes of in-degree 0, 1 and 2. Then E(0,0,0,0) = 1 and, for n >= 1, E(n,i,j,l) = Sum_{t=1..n} (-1)^(t+1)*binomial(n,t) * Sum_{s0+s1+s2+s3=t} t!/(s0!*s1!*s2!*s3!) * (m-i+s0)^s1 * (binomial(m,2)-j+s1)^s2 * (binomial(m,3)-l+s2)^s3 * E(m,i-s0,j-s1,l-s2), where m = n-t, and a(n) = Sum_{i,j,l} E(n,i,j,l).
%F A402467 (Inclusion-exclusion over sets of t sinks, as in A402238; see also Bizzaro, Serafini and Malhotra, Section 5.)
%e A402467 a(3) = 4: the digraph with no arcs and the three digraphs a -> c <- b.
%e A402467 a(5) = 2341: of the 2616 essential acyclic digraphs on 5 nodes, 275 have a node with in-degree 4.
%o A402467 (Python)
%o A402467 from math import comb
%o A402467 def aList(N):  # a(0), ..., a(N)
%o A402467     P = [{(0, 0, 0): 1}]  # P[m][(i, j, l)]: i, j, l nodes of in-degree 0, 1, 2
%o A402467     for n in range(1, N+1):
%o A402467         new = {}
%o A402467         for t in range(1, n+1):
%o A402467             m = n-t
%o A402467             for (i, j, l), w in P[m].items():
%o A402467                 for s1 in range(t+1):
%o A402467                     for s2 in range(t-s1+1):
%o A402467                         for s3 in range(t-s1-s2+1):
%o A402467                             x = (-1)**(t+1)*comb(n, t)*comb(t, s1)*comb(t-s1, s2)*comb(t-s1-s2, s3)*(m-i)**s1*(comb(m, 2)-j)**s2*(comb(m, 3)-l)**s3*w
%o A402467                             if x:
%o A402467                                 key = (i+t-s1-s2-s3, j+s1, l+s2)
%o A402467                                 new[key] = new.get(key, 0) + x
%o A402467         P.append(new)
%o A402467     return [sum(p.values()) for p in P]
%o A402467 print(aList(16))
%Y A402467 Cf. A026586 (no bound on the in-degree), A007984 (Markov equivalence classes), A402238 (in-degree at most 2).
%Y A402467 Cf. A397712 (all acyclic digraphs with in-degree at most 3).
%K A402467 nonn,new
%O A402467 0,4
